2. Fix Your Contact Form (Important)
Since you didn't use Firebase, if someone tries to send you a message right now, it won't go anywhere. We need to fix this so you don't miss out on job opportunities.

The easiest way to make the form work without a backend is to use Formspree (it's free and takes 2 minutes):

Go to Formspree.io and sign up with your GitHub or Google account.

Click "New Form" and name it "Portfolio Contact".

Formspree will give you an endpoint URL (it looks like https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxx).

Go into your VS Code, open src/components/contact.astro.

Find the <form> tag and add action="YOUR_FORMSPREE_URL" method="POST".

Commit, push to GitHub, and Vercel will automatically update your site. Now, when someone submits the form, it will send an email directly to your inbox!

